## Last text from previous session

I'll start with the required memory listing.
Now the drain API and settle-side dispatch in `dlm/v5_mount.c`:
Now the round-cap constant, placed with the barrier:
Landing the item-6C fix — the foreign-replay return value is currently discarded at both call sites, so a **failed** replay gets published as recovered:
Wrapping at the relay boundary. Build **0.11.407**, srcversion `C72F20487083A2CA52AC43C`, compiles clean.

**Item 6B is now complete** (was half-landed at 0.11.405):
- Drain API `mxfs_v5_dlm_mount_take_late_deaths` / `_defer_late_deaths` in `dlm/v5_mount.c` + `.h`, copying slot mask and node identity under `mphase_lock`.
- Barrier step (c) restructured into 4 bounded rounds that fold each drain into the next round, so a peer that dies *during* the mount is replayed by this mount instead of leaving frozen grants for `xfs_log_mount_finish` to stall on. `mount_cohort_complete` stays a single call after all rounds (sess50 cross-slice evidence rule); anything not durably replayed is handed back.
- `mxfs_v5_dlm_mount_settle` gained a phase 3a that dispatches the remainder via `v5_dispatch_slice_recovery` — the `_start_` wrapper's already-pending guard would have returned without electing a replayer.

**Item 6C exposed a second shipped defect.** `mxfs_xlog_recover_foreign_slice()` returns an error and *both* callers discarded it, so a dead peer's slice whose replay **failed** was published exactly like a successful one — CAW manifest purged, heartbeat sector zeroed, peers told it was recovered. That destroys the only two pieces of evidence that would make anyone redo the replay. Both sites now check and refuse; new `mxfs_has_log_slices(mp)` isolates the one legitimate no-replay case (unsliced FS) by testing the configuration rather than aliasing an errno.

Two RULE 6 ledger entries written (`D-MOUNT-WINDOW-PEER-DEATH-IMMEDIATE-PURGE`, `D-FOREIGN-REPLAY-FAILURE-PUBLISHED-AS-RECOVERED`), both critical/OPEN with verification plans — ledger is 41 entries, 13 open.

Also settled by line-reading, so the next session need not re-derive it: foreign replay **skips intent items entirely**, `kfree`s its shadow AIL without ever running `xlog_recover_finish`, and leaves the slice dirty for whoever next claims the slot. That confirms GPT item 3 is a real hole — the barrier publishes a slot as consumable while the dead slice's EFI/RUI/CUI/BUI intents and AGI unlinked inodes are still unprocessed.

**Criteria: NO.** Not production ready — 13 open defects, 5 critical; GPT items 3 and 4 outstanding; no rig cycle has been spent on anything since 0.11.401.

